\section*{Generalized-canonical flip termination on Kähler fourfolds}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
Generalized-canonical flip sequences with fixed rational nef data on compact Kähler fourfolds are claimed to terminate even when exceptional discrepancies equal one. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 056, 2026-10-05): A corrected finite count of low-discrepancy places first gives ordinary terminality along general points of flipped surfaces. Fixed denominator gaps and analytic surface-cycle comparisons then force a finite decrease, including zero exceptional boundary coefficients and nonnormal boundary components.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 056, 2026-10-05): The problem selects the mathematical statement summarized here, including its stated hypotheses and parameter range. The cited theorem gives a claimed proof of that assertion in full.

\subsection{Formal verification}
